    "natural_completion_before_410": true,
    "output_text": "```python\ndef is_palindrome(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check whether a string is a palindrome.\n    \n    A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards.\n    This implementation ignores case and non-alphanumeric characters.\n    \n    Args:\n        s: The input string to check.\n        \n    Returns:\n        True if the string is a palindrome, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Filter to only alphanumeric characters and convert to lowercase\n    cleaned = [char.lower() for char in s if char.isalnum()]\n    \n    # Compare the cleaned string with its reverse\n    return cleaned == cleaned[::-1]\n```\n\n**Time Complexity:** O(n), where n is the length of the input string. We iterate through the string once to filter and clean it, and then compare it with its reverse, which also takes O(n) time.\n\n**Space Complexity:** O(n), because we store the cleaned characters in a new list of size at most n.",
